e_routing已由程序完整保留，不要重复抄写全量 source_handles\". I should not copy the full list of 500+ handles into the JSON. I will just reference the key ones in the threads and rely on the system knowing the routed pool. I will only list the *excluded* ones in `excluded_source_handles`.\n\n    *Wait, another detail:* \"Return chapter_proposals (each with chapter_id, title, purpose, scope, optional excluded_source_handles, substantive_threads, supplement_requests, directed_reads) and screened_sources with non-use reasons.\"\n    So I need a `screened_sources` array at the root level of the response? No, the instruction says \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\". Usually, this means a JSON object containing these keys. But the call_id suggests a single chapter proposal. I will structure it as a single object containing `chapter_proposals` (list with one item) and `screened_sources` (list of excluded items).\n\n    *Wait, checking the prompt again:* \"Current task: chapter_proposals\". \"Return JSON only.\" \"Return chapter_proposals... and screened_sources\".\n    Okay, I will create a JSON object with keys `chapter_proposals` and `screened_sources`.\n\n    *Refining the Inosine/SCFA limitation:* The L1 outline says \"Inosine concentration data is stratified...\". The Tool Material confirms this. I must ensure the chapter plan *actively discusses* this limitation as a key finding, not just a footnote. It affects the \"Metabolite Mediators\" thread.\n\n    *Refining the Source Handles:* I will cite specific handles in the `substantive_threads` to show evidence backing, but not all 500. I will pick the most representative ones for each thread.\n\n    *Let's write the JSON.*",
